I extensively updated the spell calculation web page; the main differences
to the previous version(s) are:

  +  the complete spell table can be displayed, ordered by spell category
     first and then spell level

  +  selected spell categories may now be switched on and off individually

  +  there's an own selectable skill field for every spell category

  +  all visible spells are updated simultaneously if you change either the
     character properties, the armour, or the spell proficiency

So you'll get a quick overview how changes in your stats/armor/proficiency
will change your spellcasting abilities, and you can decide how to proceed
in an optimal way in your Nethack game.

You will find the page through this link...

     http://www.gridbug.de/spells.html

(Older versions are also still available through the formerly posted links.)

The current version is a complete rewrite and has not much in common any
more with the original source; so blame me for any errors - especially since
my JavaScript and HTML knowledge is only marginal.

I tested the calculated values a bit more thoroughly than the last version
(and noticed thereby that  sqrt((900*d)+2000)  and  10*sqrt(9*d+20)  is not
the same if sqrt is an integer function ;-) nevertheless there may still be
errors; so use the calculated data at own risk, and *don't* blame me if the
data prevents you from an ascension. :-))

The spell web page has been tested with Firefox, only, so I cannot tell or
know about potential problems with other browsers. If you detect any errors
or problems, or have any suggestion for improvement, send me a mail or post
it here.

